Unfortunately, while copying, pasting, etc., I somehow killed my
console window at this point, and thus don't have the rest of the
output, including the score, which didn't even get put in the logfile.
It boggles my mind that I could've been so careful for 133,000 turns
and then managed to botch the copy/paste, although it's probably a
better feeling than spending 133,000 turns only to get killed by
Pestilence.  Still, I made a nice screenshot before it all went wrong.
For the curious, the bag of holding included Grayswandir, Ogresmasher,
a number of wands including 3 of death (one even had charges
remaining!), and a truckload of precious gems.  I don't think I had any
fluorite stones, but the rest were covered, many in double digits.  The
cursed sack held just two holy waters; I never saw a wand of
cancellation the entire game.

I genocided L, ;, and T, and used wishes from a magic lamp from
Izchak's, a smoky potion (healing, which was nice), Croesus' throne,
and the wand of wishing in the Castle; none for artifacts.  I
polymorphed into something by accident once and never polypiled.  I was
the Hand of Elbereth and got my weapons and some spellbooks that way,
although I never cast a spell except to confuse myself.

Early game: I went to Mine Town intending to kill very few monsters and
try to get protection reasonably cheaply.  Unfortunately my trusty pet
dog died the moment I arrived in town and so I had to start fighting
for myself, naturally managing to gain levels just ahead of my ability
to buy protection.  Luckily the altar was lawful, and I tried to take
advantage.  There was also a general store here and on the level where
the mines branched off, so I spent a great deal of time hauling useless
stuff there and asking the shopkeepers to appraise things.  I also
blessed a magic lamp and managed to get my first wish, which was for
the gauntlets so I could throw Mjollnir.

By the time I got out of the mines, I was doing OK, but the game really
turned for me in the midgame when an infestation of sinks took over the
dungeon.  Despite Int 10 and Cha 9, I managed to spend an extraordinary
amount of time with the dish washers.  I had over 200 hp when I cleaned
out Fort Ludios, where I mostly relied on conflict to let the monsters
kill each other.  By the time I found Medusa's level, I was Lv30 and
chugging blessed potions of extra healing like I do Diet Pepsi at work.
I went back up and did the Quest at this point; the remainder of the
game was fairly perfunctory.

Baalzebub was bought off for 1 gold, Juiblex reduced to 1 HP with a
wand of digging while swallowed, and Vlad, Asmodeus, and Orcus went
down in HTH combat.  A wand of death I'd picked up quite a ways back
handled the Wizard each time I saw him (which wasn't very often; about
4/5 times).  Wandered up, retrieving stockpiles along the way (mostly
one giant cache on DL 13, but a few smaller ones lower down), largely
dumping items which I felt were no longer needed for gems to satisfy my
greed.  Then went up through the Planes.  The only scary moment the
whole way up was when I had to go to all three altars before finding
the right one.  Pestilence revived, caught me by surprise, and hit me
with sickness attacks; I fumbled in my bag for my unicorn horn, which
failed at first, then cured only the blindness a helpful priest of
Moloch gave me.  Luckily it worked just as I thought I was dead, and a
wand of death took care of Pestilence and Famine for the final time
when I lined the two of them up.  I guess I was wearing an amulet of
life-saving, so in retrospect I probably had it fairly under control.
;)

All in all it was quite fun, even though it took over 15 years to
manage to win.  I'm looking forward to repeating the experience, and
this time managing to survive beyond ascension as least as far as the
contents of my bag of holding...

--Mike.


